## Installation
{% if publish_pypi %}
For user installation, `{{ python_package_distribution_name }}` is currently available on the PyPi's repository, and you can
install it via `pip`:

```bash
pip install {{ python_package_distribution_name }}
```
{% endif %}
Development installation requires to clone the repository and then use [{% if package_manager == "PDM" %}PDM](https://github.com/pdm-project/pdm){% else %}uv](https://github.com/astral-sh/uv){% endif %} to install the
project as well as the main and development dependencies:

```bash
{% if git_provider == "GitHub" -%}
git clone https://github.com/{{ namespace_path }}/{{ repo_path }}.git
{% elif git_provider == "GitLab" -%}
git clone https://gitlab.com/{{ namespace_path }}/{{ repo_path }}.git
{% elif git_provider == "Azure DevOps" -%}
git clone https://dev.azure.com/{{ namespace_path }}/{{ azure_devops_project | urlencode }}/_git/{{ repo_path }}
{% elif git_provider == "Bitbucket" -%}
git clone https://bitbucket.org/{{ namespace_path }}/{{ repo_path }}.git
{% endif -%}
cd {{ python_package_distribution_name }}
{% if package_manager == "PDM" %}pdm install{% else %}uv sync{% endif %}
```
{% if project_layout == "script" %}
## Usage

Run the command:

```bash
{{ repository_name }} --name world
```
{% elif project_layout == "ml" %}
## Usage

Run the flow locally. No account or server is needed; Metaflow's local mode is the default:

```bash
python -m {{ python_package_import_name }}.flow run
```

Notebooks live in `notebooks/` and are executed by the test suite, so a notebook that stops
working fails the build. Anything placed in `data/` stays out of version control.
{% elif project_layout == "dataeng" %}
## Usage

Run the pipeline. It executes locally against the catalog in `conf/base/catalog.yml`, which
starts in memory so nothing has to be provisioned first:

```bash
python -c "from kedro.io import DataCatalog; from kedro.runner import SequentialRunner; from {{ python_package_import_name }}.pipeline import create_pipeline; SequentialRunner().run(create_pipeline(), DataCatalog())"
```

Anything placed in `data/` stays out of version control. Kedro telemetry is declined in
`.telemetry`; change it there if you want to send usage data.
{% elif project_layout == "service" %}
## Usage

Run the service locally:

```bash
uvicorn {{ python_package_import_name }}.app:app --reload
```

Then `GET /health`, or read the generated OpenAPI documentation at `/docs`.
{% endif -%}
